# heimdall-api in `local`: Docker Desktop on the Windows workstation, deployed by hand, against the
# PostgreSQL installed on Windows (database heimdall_local). The repository's own template is the
# whole file; copy it rather than this one, from your yggdrasil checkout:
#
#     cp ../heimdall-api/docker/local.env.example env/local/heimdall-api.env
#
# fill in the secrets, and deploy with YGG_SECRETS_DIR pointing at env/ (see the README). No Traefik
# in a ports environment: the API's own docker-compose.yml publishes it at API_PORT, 8080, which is
# where the local heimdall-ui calls it (http://localhost:8080). Write API_PORT=127.0.0.1:8080 to
# keep it off the network. COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME is ignored: deploy.sh names the project
# heimdall-api-local.
